TA-sanpath
====

Collects storage-path health from device-mapper-multipath (multipath -l) and iSCSI sessions (iscsiadm -m session): per-multipath active/failed path counts and path state, plus iSCSI session counts. Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype sanpath:status) and sanpath.* metrics to index=metrics (sourcetype sanpath:metrics). Hosts without multipath report 'absent' so coverage stays visible.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * multipath-tools (multipath; collection shells out to `multipath -l`) on
    hosts that use multipath; auto-detected
  * iscsi-initiator-utils (iscsiadm; session counts via `iscsiadm -m session`)
    for iSCSI session counts; auto-detected
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="sanpath:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="sanpath:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="sanpath.*" by host
  | mstats avg("sanpath.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=sanpath:status  (per-multipath path state; iSCSI session list count)
Metrics: sanpath.<mp>_active_paths / sanpath.<mp>_failed_paths / sanpath.iscsi_session_count
Dashboards: TA-Sanpath > Sanpath Overview / Sanpath Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-sanpath/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * `multipath -l` output only exists when the multipathd daemon is running and paths are present.
  * A failed/empty `multipath -l` while /sys/class/scsi_device and /run/multipathd.socket exist
    reports 'permission_or_daemon_issue' instead of silently pretending multipath is absent.
  * Local-disk hosts are expected to report 'absent'.

License
-------
SOURCE-AVAILABLE (see LICENSE) - free personal, educational and evaluation
use; commercial or production use requires a paid license from BentleyPC
LLC (https://www.bentleypc.com/TA-sanpath).

Enter your key (format BP-...) after purchase using EITHER method:

  1. Splunk Web: open the app, click "License" in the nav, click a row to
     open the key entry page, paste the key and Save.

  2. File (headless / forwarder friendly): create the file
     $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-sanpath/local/license.conf with:

         [settings]
         telemetry_enabled = 1
         key = BP-xxxxxxxxxxxx

     No restart required - the hourly beacon reads this file on every run.

Set telemetry_enabled = 0 to keep the key for validation but pause all
outbound beacons. The beacon sends only: license key, hostname, app name
and app version to the BentleyPC license API (see api_base in
default/license.conf). It is telemetry only - never a license check that
blocks functionality.
